lesson: 110
title: Review: fractions and shapes together
stars: 2
explain: Some problems need two steps: first the area of a rectangle, then a fraction of that area.
explain: A garden 8 m long and 6 m wide has 8 × 6 = 48 square meters. If one third is planted with flowers, that is 48 ÷ 3 = 16, so 48 − 16 = 32 square meters have no flowers.
vars: a=name l=3..20 w=2..15 p=3..6 d=2..9
need: l > w
need: l * w % p == 0
answer: l * w - l * w / p
exercise: A rectangular garden is {l} m long and {w} m wide. {a} plants flowers on one {p.ordwords} of it. How many square meters have no flowers?
exercise: A rectangle of {l} by {w} unit squares is drawn. One {p.ordwords} of the squares are colored. How many squares are not colored?
exercise: {a} has a rectangular piece of paper {l} cm by {w} cm. {a.He} cuts off one {p.ordwords} of its area. How many square cm are left?
exercise: A floor is {l} m long and {w} m wide. One {p.ordwords} of it is covered with a rug. How many square meters of the floor are uncovered?
exercise: A rectangular field {w} m wide and {l} m long is split into {p} equal parts, and one part is sown with wheat. How many square meters are not sown?
test: {a} tiles a floor that is {w} m wide and {l} m long with square tiles 1 m by 1 m. {a.He} has already laid one {p.ordwords} of them. How many tiles are still to be laid?
test: A rectangular park measures {l} m by {w} m and has {d} gates. One {p.ordwords} of the park is a pond. How many square meters of the park are land?
test: How many unit squares stay white if one {p.ordwords} of a {w} by {l} rectangle of unit squares is painted?
test: A chocolate bar costs {d} dollars and has {w} rows of {l} pieces. {a} eats one {p.ordwords} of the pieces. How many pieces are left?
exercise: A rectangular lawn in Ohio is {l} m long and {w} m wide. One {p.ordwords} of it is covered by a shed. How many square meters of lawn are left?
exercise: {a} paints one {p.ordwords} of a rectangular wall {w} m high and {l} m long. How many square meters are still unpainted?
exercise: A rectangle is made of {w} by {l} unit squares, and one {p.ordwords} of the squares are shaded. How many squares are not shaded?
exercise: A rectangular field in Devon is {l} m by {w} m. Sheep graze on one {p.ordwords} of it. How many square meters are not grazed?
exercise: {a} in Sydney has a rectangular sheet of card {l} cm long and {w} cm wide. {a.He} uses one {p.ordwords} of its area. How many square cm of card remain?
exercise: How many square meters of a {l} m by {w} m rectangular yard are left after one {p.ordwords} of it is paved?
exercise: A chocolate bar is a rectangle with {w} rows of {l} squares. {a} gives away one {p.ordwords} of the squares. How many squares does {a.he} still have?
exercise: One {p.ordwords} of a rectangular floor {l} m long and {w} m wide is under a carpet. How much of the floor, in square meters, is bare?
test: In Alberta, {a} plants potatoes on one {p.ordwords} of a garden that is {w} m wide and {l} m long. The rest is grass. How many square meters are grass?
test: A rectangular pool cover is {l} m by {w} m, and {d} lights shine around the pool. One {p.ordwords} of the cover is rolled back. How many square meters of the cover still lie on the pool?
test: A baking tray holds {w} rows of {l} square brownies. One {p.ordwords} of the brownies are eaten at a party in Auckland. How many brownies are left?
test: How many square cm are left of a {w} cm by {l} cm rectangle of paper after one {p.ordwords} of it is cut away?
test: A school playground in Cardiff measures {l} m by {w} m and has {d} benches. One {p.ordwords} of it is a basketball court. How many square meters are not the court?
test: {a} colors one {p.ordwords} of the unit squares in a grid {l} squares long and {w} squares wide. How many squares stay blank?
exercise: garden {l} by {w} m, {a} put flowers on one {p.ordwords}. how many square m got no flowers
exercise: paper {l+1} — no wait, {l} cm by {w} cm, cut off one {p.ordwords} of it. square cm left?
exercise: grid {l} by {w} squares, one {p.ordwords} coloured. Sam says {l*w/p} not coloured. nah, what's the real answer
exercise: playground {l} m x {w} m, got {d} benches n one {p.ordwords} of it is the court. how many square m ain't court
test: tray's {w} rows of {l} brownies, one {p.ordwords} got eaten lol. how many left then
test: {a}'s grid is {l} long {w} wide, colours one {p.ordwords}, rest blank — how many blank? used {d} crayons btw
test: field {l} m by {w+2} m, no sorry, {w} m. one {p.ordwords} is for footy. how much ain't for footy, square m
exam: It is given that a rectangular garden measures {l} m by {w} m and that flowers are planted on one {p.ordwords} of its area. Determine the area, in square metres, devoid of flowers.
exam: Ascertain the number of squares not coloured in a rectangle of {l} by {w} unit squares, one {p.ordwords} of the squares having been coloured.
exam: Whereas a rectangular floor of {l} m by {w} m is covered with a rug over one {p.ordwords} of its area, state the uncovered area in square metres.
exam: Compute the area remaining when one {p.ordwords} is deducted from the area of a rectangle of {l} units by {w} units, expressed in square units.
exercise: Grandma passed away and left a vegetable patch {l} m long and {w} m wide. {a} plants flowers on one {p.ordwords} of it in her memory. How many square meters have no flowers?
exercise: A farm's field is {l} m by {w} m. In "challenging trading conditions" one {p.ordwords} of it was sold off. How many square meters does the farm still own?
test: the dog "did its business" on a {p.ordwords} of the {l} by {w} m lawn, mucky pup. how many square m are still clean
